        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 7:37 p.m. Central Daylight Time Sunday, Environment Canada has updated a tornado warning for Westman Manitoba. Extra care and attention should be exercised. The following localities are included in the warning: Brandon, Forrest, Chater, Oakland-Wawanesa, Holland, Norfolk Treherne and Treesbank. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
        </parameter>
